Happy Friday! Sam Altman said AI would make the one-person billion-dollar c=
ompany possible. A guy in LA selling weight-loss drugs from his living room=
 just proved him right. $20K startup cost. Two months to build. One employe=
e: his brother. $1.8 billion in projected annual sales. Elsewhere, OpenAI b=
ought a talk show, Google gave away its best models and Perplexity showed a=
n AI doing your taxes. Here is everything you need to know today. Medvi: So=
lo founder builds $1.8B company with AI and $20K OpenAI buys TBPN in its fi=
rst media acquisition Google drops Gemma 4 under Apache 2.0 for the first t=
ime Perplexity Computer files your taxes live on camera A Solo Founder Used=
 AI To Build A $1.8 Billion Company Matthew Gallagher spent $20,000 and two=
 months launching Medvi, a telehealth startup selling GLP-1 drugs online. H=
is only full-time hire is his brother. The company is on pace for $1.8 bill=
ion in annual sales. The stack: ChatGPT, Claude and Grok for code. Midjourn=
ey and Runway for ads. ElevenLabs and custom agents for customer service. D=
octors and prescriptions outsourced to CareValidate and OpenLoop. The numbe=
rs: $401M revenue in year one. Contract engineers and account managers fill=
 the gaps. The core operation was built by one person. The sign: Altman pre=
dicted this in 2024. Gallagher delivered it. And the product has nothing to=
 do with AI. It is a drug distribution business running on AI infrastructur=
e. GLP-1 demand is extraordinary and the telehealth regulatory window may n=
ot stay open forever. But the operational model is what matters. What used =
to take 50 people, office space and millions in funding can now be assemble=
d by one person moving fast enough. GenAI Works Academy is now live Practic=
al courses on ChatGPT, Claude, Cursor, Perplexity, Deep Seek and more, taug=
ht by instructors who actually use them in production. Whether you want to =
build faster, automate your work or figure out which tools are worth your t=
ime, there's a course for it. What's inside: Prompt engineering for profess=
ionals Claude Code from zero to shipping AI-powered marketing, data science=
 and business strategy Beginner to advanced tracks across every major platf=
orm No filler. No theory-only lectures. Just the skills that are actually m=
oving careers forward right now. Explore GenAI Academy =E2=86=92 OpenAI Jus=
t Bought A Talk Show OpenAI acquired TBPN for a reported low hundreds of mi=
llions. First media acquisition by any AI lab. The show: 70,000 viewers per=
 episode. Daily live on YouTube and X. Required watching for Silicon Valley=
 founders and executives. $30M revenue run rate. Launched 17 months ago. Th=
e deal: TBPN's 11-person team reports to OpenAI's global affairs chief Chri=
s Lehane. Ad business dropped. Editorial independence retained. The play: O=
penAI has taken public hits all year. Rather than fighting it through press=
 releases, they bought the room where the tech conversation actually happen=
s. This is a reputation play. OpenAI has taken sustained criticism this yea=
r and buying TBPN gives them a direct line to the founders and operators wh=
o shape tech sentiment daily. Whether the show can maintain credibility und=
er corporate ownership is the obvious question, but killing its authenticit=
y would defeat the purpose. Google Open-Sources Its Most Capable Models Yet=
 Google DeepMind dropped Gemma 4. Four open models. Apache 2.0 licence. Fir=
st time the Gemma line has been fully open for commercial use. The range: 2=
B, 4B, 26B MoE and 31B. All handle vision, code and multi-step agent tasks.=
 Smallest variants add voice and run offline on a phone. The shift: Previou=
s Gemma releases used a restrictive custom licence that pushed enterprise d=
evelopers towards Qwen and Mistral. Apache 2.0 removes that friction entire=
ly. The context: Chinese labs have dominated open-source AI for the past ye=
ar. This week, two US releases pushed back: Arcee AI Trinity-Large and Gemm=
a 4. Google is going more open while its Chinese rivals go closed. The timi=
ng matters. Open-source AI has been a Chinese-dominated story for the past =
year, with Qwen and DeepSeek setting the pace. Two major US releases in one=
 week signals that dynamic is shifting. Google choosing to go more permissi=
ve while its rivals tighten up could reshape where enterprise developers pl=
ace their bets. Perplexity Computer Will Do Your Taxes April 15 is approach=
ing. Perplexity dropped a demo of its Computer agent preparing a federal ta=
x return. 1.9 million views. How it works: Upload documents, answer questio=
ns, watch the agent fill out IRS forms. Perplexity claims it retrieves and =
applies the current tax code live. Why it matters: This is not a chatbot gi=
ving tax tips. It is a browser agent navigating forms and entering data. Th=
e most tangible demo of computer-use AI aimed at normal people so far. The =
caveat: Double-check everything. Preparation assistance, not a replacement =
for professional review. Computer-use agents have been a talking point for =
months. Most demos have felt like developer previews. Showing an AI handlin=
g the single most universally dreaded admin task of the year is a smarter s=
ell than any benchmark chart. Tool of the Day: StoryMotion Turn static diag=
rams into hand-drawn animated videos. Sketch on a canvas, control when each=
 element appears, export as video. No motion design skills needed. Open sto=
rymotion.video Sketch or pick a template Add effects and adjust timing Expo=
rt and drop into your deck, course or post Try it yourself: storymotion.vid=
eo Light Bytes Artemis II launches: Crew of four headed for the Moon. If su=
ccessful, they will travel further than any humans in history. Sanctuary AI=
 robotic hand: Hydraulic hand manipulates a cube ten consecutive times at t=
he fingertips with no palm support. Zero-shot transfer from simulation. Byt=
eDance Seedance 2.0: AI video generator now broadly available. Top of Artif=
icial Analysis' video leaderboards. Alibaba Qwen3.6-Plus: Reasoning model r=
ivalling Opus 4.5 on coding benchmarks. 1M-token context. Multimodal. Micro=
soft MAI-Transcribe-1: Speech-to-text topping accuracy across 25 languages.=
 Public preview. Cursor 3: Full rebuild. Multi-workspace. Parallel agents a=
cross repos. Microsoft lost OpenAI: How one of the most preventable corpora=
te mishaps of the decade cost Microsoft its largest customer and US governm=
ent trust.
